Size the array descriptor from Descriptor_Size (riscv64)

The vectors keep their elements behind a descriptor holding the bounds, as GNAT
does for an array reached through a thin pointer, and checked at elaboration
that the descriptor is exactly the two Naturals of Array_Bounds:

    pragma Assert (Array_Bounds'Size = Elements_Array'Descriptor_Size, ...);

GNAT pads the descriptor so that the array stays aligned.  For element types
that need 16-byte alignment (AdaSAT's DPLL Watcher on riscv64) the descriptor
is 16 bytes, not 8, and the assertion fails when the package is elaborated:

    raised ADA.ASSERTIONS.ASSERTION_ERROR : Unexpected size for array bounds

Derive the room reserved in front of the elements from Descriptor_Size, so
that the elements are 16-byte aligned (the allocator's 16 plus 16), and require
only that the descriptor is at least the bounds.  The bounds are written at
the start of the descriptor, as before.  For every other element type the
descriptor is 8 bytes and nothing changes.  Checked on riscv64 with a 16-byte
aligned element: bounds 1 .. 5 and five correctly aligned elements.

--- a/src/adasat-vectors.adb
+++ b/src/adasat-vectors.adb
@@ -15,8 +15,13 @@
    end record;
 
    pragma Assert
-     (Array_Bounds'Size = Elements_Array'Descriptor_Size,
+     (Elements_Array'Descriptor_Size >= Array_Bounds'Size,
       "Unexpected size for array bounds");
+   --  GNAT pads the descriptor (the bounds) of an array reached through a thin
+   --  pointer so that the array itself stays aligned: when the elements need
+   --  more than 8 bytes of alignment (16 for some records on riscv64) the
+   --  descriptor is larger than the bounds.  The bounds are the first bytes of
+   --  the descriptor, which starts Descriptor_Size bytes before the elements.
 
    type Thin_Unconstrained_Array_Access is access all Elements_Array;
    for Thin_Unconstrained_Array_Access'Size use Standard'Address_Size;
@@ -29,7 +34,10 @@
    type Fat_Unconstrained_Array_Access is access all Elements_Array;
 
    El_Size : constant size_t := Elements_Array'Component_Size / Storage_Unit;
-   Bd_Size : constant size_t := Array_Bounds'Size / Storage_Unit;
+   Bd_Size : constant size_t :=
+     size_t (Elements_Array'Descriptor_Size) / Storage_Unit;
+   --  Room for the whole descriptor (bounds and padding) in front of the
+   --  elements
    Offset  : constant Storage_Count := Storage_Count (Bd_Size);
 
    --------------
